  "headline_interpretation": "Both human Inspiration4 skin and mouse hindlimb gastrocnemius post-flight strongly down-regulate translation/proteostasis machinery (ribosomal proteins, eIF complexes, NMD, SRP-mediated cotranslational targeting, rRNA processing). The mouse skin transcriptome instead UP-regulates the same Hallmark/Reactome subset, breaking direct tissue matching. On this 25-pathway Hallmark-dominated overlap the skin-to-skin transfer signal is therefore swamped by a stronger conserved muscle/skin proteostasis suppression axis driven by ribosomal-protein genes."
